k><name>OSE, ASUKA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Novel fetal genes (fls353 and fls485) are successfully isolated from cDNAs orginating in human fetal liver. These genes are expressed specifically in tissues typified by fetal tissues which are seemingly rich in undifferentiated cells or cells under vigorous differentiation and proliferation. Also, these genes are highly expressed in various cancer cells. These proteins and genes encoding the same are usable as tools for developing drugs against tumor.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Selon l'invention, on a isolé avec succès des nouveaux gènes de foetus (fls353 et fls485) à partir d'ADNc provenant d'un foie de foetus humain. Ces gènes sont exprimés de manière spécifique dans des tissus, généralement des tissus de foetus qui sont en apparence riches en cellules se différentiant et proliférant rapidement. De même, ces gènes sont fortement exprimés dans diverses cellules cancéreuses. On peut utiliser ces protéines et les gènes les codant en tant qu'outils de mise au point de médicaments contre des tumeurs.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>